 "notes": "Body coordinates follow SPEC (x=0 string centreline, y=0 butt on centreline, bass = -x). Nut (fretboard side) is at y=83.21, 22nd fret y=37.98 = body edge on centreline. Body outline includes the straight neck-joint edge x=-3.07..3.07 at y=37.98; the neck (5.6 cm wide at the fretboard end) enters there. BEVELS: every bevel entry has 'innerEdge' = the polyline where the flat face meets the bevel (width = horizontal distance to outline, median value given, 'widthMax' too); depth = vertical drop at the outer edge on that face. Front: bass side from the lower bout (~y 2) all around the bass horn into the cutaway (constant ~1.97 cm wide), treble side from the waist (y~22.6) around the treble horn into the cutaway (0.9 -> 1.6 cm, widest near the horn). No front bevel around the butt/treble lower bout where the controls sit. Back: bass half continuous from the butt centre to the bass horn/cutaway (~1.8 cm, up to 2.8 near the waist), treble half from y~16.4 to the treble horn (~1.35 cm). Model bevels as a planar chamfer from innerEdge down to the rim; the remaining vertical rim at a double-bevelled section is 3.49 - 2*0.79 = 1.91 cm, with R0.32 edges. The bevels die out to zero width at their ends and meet at the horn tips. PICKGUARD: 1961-62 small 5-ply black guard (b/w/b/w/b), ~0.25 cm thick, on the treble side; its tab (x=1.96) sits between the two pickup rings. Bridge: ABR-1 posts at tomPosts (bass post slightly further back), stopbar studs 8.26 apart at y=16.22. Pickup 'size' is the cover (6.9 x 3.8); black rings 8.4 x 4.4. CONTROLS: knobs listed volume row first (row nearer the bridge: inner, outer) then tone row (inner, outer); top-hat knobs ~2.5 cm diameter. Toggle is in a round 'RHYTHM/TREBLE' ring (~3.4 cm) on the top between the pickguard tail and the knobs, lever throws across the strings (angleDeg 0 = along x). Jack is a front-mounted jack on the top below the tone knobs. Strap buttons: [0,0] on the butt edge; [0,36.4] is on the BACK of the neck heel. HEADSTOCK: outline/posts measured in the headstock face plane, 3+3 (posts listed E A D on bass side from nut outwards, then G B e from tip back to nut), face tilted back 17 deg starting just past the nut. Open-book top with centre dip at y=17.73; max length 17.95 cm; width 4.28 at the nut, 7.7 at the wing tips. Known discrepancies: the Stouffs plan places the butt ~1.8 cm further from the bridge (rejected by photo + other templates); the product photo suggests the real body may be ~2% smaller overall than the templates (33.3 wide)."
